---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Scavland Weapons Database — Complete Firearms & Attachment Stats" description="The complete Scavland weapons database: 25+ firearms, ammo calibers, 300+ attachment slots, ballistics, recoil control, durability, and workbench repair recipes." keywords="Scavland weapons, Scavland attachments, firearms database, weapon stats, gun modification, ammo calibers, weapon repair, Scavland wiki" canonical="/weapons/">
  <Fragment slot="schema">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Scavland Wiki', item: 'https://scavland.wiki/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Weapons & Attachments', item: 'https://scavland.wiki/weapons/' }
      ]
    })} />
  </Fragment>
  <article class="article-shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:0.82rem;color:var(--text-muted,#888);margin-bottom:1.25rem;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.4rem;align-items:center;">
      <a href="/" style="color:var(--acid,#b9e86c);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Scavland Wiki</a>
      <span style="opacity:0.4;">/</span>
      <span style="color:#bbb;">Weapons &amp; Attachments</span>
    </nav>
    <header class="article-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Arsenal Database · Updated August 31, 2026</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Weapons &amp; Attachments</h1>
      <p class="lede">Comprehensive field catalog of all 25+ firearms, 300+ modular attachment configurations, ammo ballistics, recoil curves, and workbench maintenance in Zalesye.</p>
      <span class="evidence">Evidence: Official Verified Baseline</span>
    </header>

    <div class="article-layout">
      <div class="article-content">
        <div class="media-strip" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin:0 0 24px;">
          <figure style="margin:0;">
            <img src="/images/screenshots/steam_ss_01.webp" alt="Official Scavland tactical firefight and weapon handling" style="width:100%;height:180px;border-radius:4px;border:1px solid var(--line);object-fit:cover;" loading="lazy"/>
            <figcaption class="caption">Tactical firefight and ballistic spread during overworld exploration</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure style="margin:0;">
            <img src="/images/screenshots/steam_ss_10.webp" alt="Official Scavland weapon modification and attachment station" style="width:100%;height:180px;border-radius:4px;border:1px solid var(--line);object-fit:cover;" loading="lazy"/>
            <figcaption class="caption">Modular attachment slots: optics, muzzle devices, handguards, and magazines</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="quick-answer" style="margin-bottom:32px;">
          <strong>Key Gunplay Systems</strong>
          Firearms in Scavland are governed by four interacting systems: Caliber Penetration, Modular Attachments (300+ parts), Durability Degradation, and Dynamic Jam Probability. Choosing the right tool for the environment (tight bunker hallways vs. wide open radioactive marshes) is the single most critical survival skill.
        </div>

        <h2 id="roster">Firearms Roster &amp; Caliber Specifications</h2>
        <p>Below is the verified weapon baseline organized by tactical role, effective engagement distance, and standard ammunition types.</p>

        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0;">
          <table class="facts" style="width:100%;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="border-bottom:2px solid var(--line);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);">
                <th style="padding:10px;text-align:left;color:var(--acid);font:.72rem 'IBM Plex Mono';">CATEGORY</th>
                <th style="padding:10px;text-align:left;color:var(--acid);font:.72rem 'IBM Plex Mono';">REPRESENTATIVE</th>
                <th style="padding:10px;text-align:left;color:var(--acid);font:.72rem 'IBM Plex Mono';">CALIBER</th>
                <th style="padding:10px;text-align:left;color:var(--acid);font:.72rem 'IBM Plex Mono';">OPTIMAL RANGE</th>
                <th style="padding:10px;text-align:left;color:var(--acid);font:.72rem 'IBM Plex Mono';">MOD SLOTS</th>
                <th style="padding:10px;text-align:left;color:var(--acid);font:.72rem 'IBM Plex Mono';">TACTICAL ROLE</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-weight:700;color:var(--acid);">Sidearm</td>
                <td>Makarov PM / TT-33</td>
                <td><code>9x18mm / 7.62x25mm</code></td>
                <td>0 – 15m</td>
                <td>Muzzle, Mag, Grip</td>
                <td>Lightweight emergency sidearm; 0 weight penalty. Essential backup when primary rifle jams.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-weight:700;color:var(--acid);">SMG</td>
                <td>PP-19 Bizon / MP5</td>
                <td><code>9x19mm Parabellum</code></td>
                <td>5 – 25m</td>
                <td>Optic, Suppressor, Drum</td>
                <td>High burst DPS against unarmored mutant swarms. High ammo consumption.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-weight:700;color:var(--acid);">Assault Rifle</td>
                <td>AK-74M / AS Val</td>
                <td><code>5.45x39mm / 9x39mm</code></td>
                <td>15 – 60m</td>
                <td>Full Modular (6 slots)</td>
                <td>All-around wasteland workhorse. High armor penetration and manageable vertical kick.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-weight:700;color:var(--acid);">Battle Rifle</td>
                <td>AK-47 / AK-50 Improvised</td>
                <td><code>7.62x39mm / .50 BMG</code></td>
                <td>20 – 80m</td>
                <td>Optic, Brake, Heavy Stock</td>
                <td>Massive single-shot stopping power against armored Warden patrols and mutant brutes.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-weight:700;color:var(--acid);">Shotgun</td>
                <td>TOZ-34 / Saiga-12</td>
                <td><code>12-Gauge Buck / Slug</code></td>
                <td>0 – 12m</td>
                <td>Choke, Extended Tube</td>
                <td>King of close-quarters bunker corridor clearance. High stagger chance against charging beasts.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-weight:700;color:var(--acid);">Sniper / DMR</td>
                <td>Mosin-Nagant / SVD Dragunov</td>
                <td><code>7.62x54mmR</code></td>
                <td>50 – 120m+</td>
                <td>4x/8x Scope, Cheek Pad</td>
                <td>Long-range scout weapon. Eliminates sniper lookouts before entering contested outposts.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2 id="attachments">300+ Attachment Customization System</h2>
        <p>Modifying a weapon alters its weight, ergonomics (aim-down-sight speed), recoil impulse, and sound profile:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Muzzle Slots:</strong> Suppressors eliminate muzzle flash and shrink sound detection radius by 75%, preventing nearby mutant nests from waking up. Flash hiders and compensators reduce recoil climb during automatic spray.</li>
          <li><strong>Optic Rails:</strong> Reflex sights offer wide field-of-view for bunker raids; 4x PSO-1 and variable scopes provide precise hit registration through foggy mist zones.</li>
          <li><strong>Foregrips &amp; Laser Modules:</strong> Angled grips stabilize horizontal sway, while underbarrel tactical lights illuminate pitch-black Soviet bunker corridors.</li>
          <li><strong>Magazines &amp; Drums:</strong> High-capacity drum magazines increase total ammunition pool between reloads at the cost of slower reload animations and weapon handling speed.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="article-media">
          <img src="/images/screenshots/steam_ss_06.webp" alt="Combat stance and aiming in Scavland" />
          <p class="caption">Long-range target engagement across foggy sector borders</p>
        </div>

        <h2 id="durability">Durability, Jams &amp; Maintenance</h2>
        <p>Firing weapons in bad weather or neglected condition leads to dangerous mechanical jams:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>100% – 70% Condition:</strong> Pristine operation. 0% jam probability. Maximum ballistic accuracy.</li>
          <li><strong>69% – 40% Condition:</strong> Moderate barrel fouling. Slight accuracy deviation and occasional delayed hammer strike.</li>
          <li><strong>Under 40% Condition:</strong> Critical wear. High chance of cartridge stovepiping or failure to feed during automatic fire.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To repair and maintain firearms, use <strong>Gun Cleaning Oil</strong> in the field or visit a Safehouse <strong>Weapon Workbench</strong> with scrap springs and gun parts.</p>

        <h2 id="next">Related Guides</h2>
        <div class="related-grid">
          <a href="/guide/scavland-weapon-repair-and-durability/"><strong>Weapon Repair &amp; Jams</strong><br/>Step-by-step field cleaning and workbench repair guide</a>
          <a href="/factions/"><strong>10 Factions &amp; Vendors</strong><br/>Faction weapon shops and loyalty discount tiers</a>
          <a href="/guide/scavland-beginner-guide/"><strong>Beginner Guide</strong><br/>Essential first-run survival, inventory and looting</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <strong>On this page</strong>
        <a href="#roster">Firearms Roster</a>
        <a href="#attachments">300+ Attachments</a>
        <a href="#durability">Durability &amp; Jams</a>
        <a href="#next">Related Guides</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
